IMPORT prelude

-- Working time of soldiers: Soldatengesetz (SG) § 30c, with the exemption in Soldatenarbeitszeitverordnung (SAZV) § 1(2) and its Anlage,
-- the power the exemption rests on (SG § 30c(6) with § 93(2) no. 7) and the citation requirement of Grundgesetz Art. 80(1) sentence 3.
-- Law layer. The seat layer is saz-seat.l4. Target compiler: main.
-- Every quotation is a verbatim slice of a deposited source in ../../registers/source-bundle/, checked with srcrefs.py.
-- German is the only authoritative language; English names are glosses.

§ `Facts about a soldier`

-- A soldier serving in the German armed forces. Each field is a fact the soldier can state.
DECLARE `Soldier` HAS
    `serves within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- SAZV § 1(1); SG § 30c(1) sentence 1
    `establishment`                                                                      IS A STRING   -- the name of the establishment where the soldier is posted, exactly as the annex prints it, or an empty text if none
    `has been transferred or assigned there to perform international or supranational tasks` IS A BOOLEAN  -- SAZV § 1(2)
    `is performing an activity listed in section 30c subsection 4`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- a characterisation asked as a fact: operations, disaster aid, multi-day sea voyages and so on
    `overtime hours ordered or approved this month`                                       IS A NUMBER   -- hours beyond the regular working time, officially ordered or approved (SG § 30c(2) sentence 2)
    `hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible`                   IS A NUMBER   -- SG § 30c(2) sentence 5 ("soweit")
    `has a long-term working-time account`                                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- SAZV § 1(3)

§ `Anlage zu § 1 Absatz 2 SAZV: the establishments`

-- The annex as printed on gesetze-im-internet.de on 2026-11-02 (Fundstelle BGBl. 2025 Nr. 78, S. 4 to 6): 88 numbered rows.
-- The gazette (BGBl. 2025 I Nr. 78, Art. 5 No. 7) prints the same 88 rows.
-- Generated mechanically from lines 4 to 91 of sazv-anlage.txt; the tests assert the count and row 27.
DECLARE `Annex row` HAS
    `number`          IS A NUMBER
    `establishment`   IS A STRING
    `state`           IS A STRING

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      establishment IS A STRING
      state IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Annex row`
`an annex row` n establishment state MEANS
    `Annex row` WITH `number` IS n, `establishment` IS establishment, `state` IS state

